WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.472 --> 00:00:03.925
Every AI lab ships its own agent, in its own app.

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:08.113
Then one hits its usage limit, and your work just waits.

3
00:00:08.255 --> 00:00:10.660
And it is all stuck on one machine.

4
00:00:11.226 --> 00:00:16.868
SpecWithCode puts Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, Gemini and more in one window.

5
00:00:17.358 --> 00:00:19.198
Tell the coordinator what you want.

6
00:00:19.528 --> 00:00:22.943
It plans, briefs and routes. Threads do the work.

7
00:00:23.396 --> 00:00:26.038
Each thread owns its job and keeps its context,

8
00:00:26.604 --> 00:00:29.208
so a follow-up goes to the thread that owns it.

9
00:00:29.623 --> 00:00:34.038
Hit a usage limit, and the work continues on another provider, with its context.

10
00:00:34.528 --> 00:00:38.679
Connect your Mac, Linux and Windows machines, with no port forwarding.

11
00:00:39.245 --> 00:00:41.792
The coordinator starts threads on the ones you allow.

12
00:00:42.264 --> 00:00:46.547
And one Chrome extension serves every agent, in your real Chrome profile.

13
00:00:47.075 --> 00:00:49.245
Claude Code alone runs Claude.

14
00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:53.208
T3 Code pauses until the reset, or until you switch by hand.

15
00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:57.311
SpecWithCode switches for you, and keeps your whole team working.

16
00:00:57.925 --> 00:01:02.972
Free for Apple silicon Macs, Windows and Linux. At specwithcode.com.
